.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBRangeSlider\fR: a slider with two thumbs that selects a range (\fBlo..=hi\fR) of values; the sibling of \fBscale\fR, drawn with the same rail and handle styling (\fBstyle::slider\fR) with the accent fill between the thumbs.
.PP
A thin applier of \fBprimitives::range\fR: the \fBTrack\fR decides which thumb a press grabs, where a thumb may go (the other thumb stops it, or is pushed, and the minimum gap holds), the step it snaps to and what each key does. The application owns the \fB(lo, hi)\fR pair and updates it from \fBon_change\fR; without \fBon_change\fR, or with \fBdisabled\fR, the slider is drawn dimmed and ignores input.
.PP
.nf
.RS
range_slider(0.0..=100.0, (self.lo, self.hi), Message::Range)
    .step(5.0)
    .min_gap(10.0)
.RE
.fi
.PP
Each thumb is a focus stop: arrows step it, \fBPageUp\fR/\fBPageDown\fR move ten steps, \fBHome\fR and \fBEnd\fR go to the ends. Pressing on a thumb drags it; pressing on the rail moves the nearest thumb there and keeps dragging it.
